.TH _PRINTF 3 "November 2025" "Custom C Library" "User Functions"
.SH NAME
_printf \- custom implementation of the standard printf function
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include "main.h"

.B int _printf(const char *format, ...);
.SH DESCRIPTION
The
.B _printf
function produces output according to a format string. It writes output to the standard output stream (stdout) using the
.B write
system call.

The format string is composed of ordinary characters and conversion specifiers, which begin with a '%' character and define how subsequent arguments are formatted.

Supported conversion specifiers:

.TP
.B %c
Prints a single character.

.TP
.B %s
Prints a null-terminated string.

.TP
.B %%
Prints a literal percent sign.

.TP
.B %d, %i
Prints a signed decimal integer.

Unsupported features:

- Flag characters (e.g., '+', ' ', '#')
- Field width and precision
- Length modifiers (e.g., 'l', 'h')
- Floating-point formats

.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns the number of characters printed (excluding the null byte used to end output to strings).

Returns
.B -1
if the format string is NULL or ends with an incomplete '%' specifier.

.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
_printf("Hello, %s\\n", "Joshua");   // Output: Hello, Joshua
_printf("Value: %d\\n", 42);         // Output: Value: 42
_printf("Percent: %%\\n");           // Output: Percent: %
.fi

.SH SEE ALSO
printf(3), write(2), va_start(3), va_arg(3), va_end(3)
